# <modbus-client> in bennu mode against the stock modbus-server (ww-7mw.1). The DUT is the client (stock/client-modbus.xml: bennu's sample
# modbus-client.xml plus two points the server lacks and one with the default range); the stock server (stock/server-modbus.xml, a copy of bennu's sample)
# runs beside it under stock/servectl.py, so peer.sh can stop and start it. peer.sh drives the client's command interface
# (stock/probe_cmdif.py) and check.sh wants the transcript, replies and Modbus bytes, equal to the stock client's
# (stock/client-modbus.golden). Record that golden: conformance/stock/run-stock.sh modbus-client
CFG=${CFG:-${here:-/conformance}/stock/client-modbus.xml}
STOCK_CMD='cd /tmp && bennu-field-device --f /tmp/cfg.xml'
DUT_EXTRA="conformance/stock/servectl.py:/tmp/servectl.py conformance/stock/server-modbus.xml:/tmp/server.xml"
DUT_PRE='python3 /tmp/servectl.py 5999 bennu-field-device --f /tmp/server.xml'
WARMUP=3
CAPTURE_FILTER='tcp port 5502'
PROTO_FILTER='mbtcp'
TSHARK_EXTRA='-d tcp.port==5502,mbtcp'
# requests to the stopped server are refused, and the exceptions are the point of half the cases
EXPERT_ALLOW='Connection reset|Connection finish|Exception returned|Cannot classify packet type'
ZEEK_LOAD=''
